    "result_text": "The full test suite is green: **32 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the audit-on-create requirement in the owner creation endpoint (`POST /api/owners`), handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`.\n\n**Changes to `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:**\n\n1. Added a dedicated SLF4J logger named `AUDIT`:\n   ```java\n   private static final org.slf4j.Logger AUDIT = org.slf4j.LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\");\n   ```\n\n2. Emitted the audit line immediately after the owner is persisted (so the generated `id`, along with the already-assigned `customerCode` and adjusted `registrationDate`, are all populated):\n   ```java\n   this.clinicService.saveOwner(owner);\n   AUDIT.info(\"Owner created: id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={}\",\n       owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate());\n   ```\n\nThis satisfies `Cp21Tests`, which captures the `AUDIT` logger and asserts a single log line contains the owner id, customerCode, and registrationDate as substrings. The observed line was e.g. `AUDIT - Owner created: id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-08-12`. All 32 tests across the suite pass.",
